```

This strengthening is sound. Here is the contour detail behind the root's
degree count, including the fact that E_r is oblique and its image is not
literally the bare grade r.

Insert a parameter theta in `h_eff(theta)=h-i theta gamma epsilon^2 Gamma`.
At theta=0, `E_r(0)U_H P=Q_r U_H P=0` for r>0. Expand the uniformly convergent
resolvent and canonical-column series in epsilon and theta. After that exact
theta-zero cancellation, every surviving word contains at least one Gamma
insertion, costing epsilon degree two. Its E_r contour integral can have a
nonzero residue only if its resolvent word visits bare grade r somewhere.
Starting at the rightmost P, reaching that visit costs at least r adjacent
T factors. C and Gamma preserve grade. Terms from the canonical polar series
also consist of such graded words and cannot reduce that number of hops.
Thus each surviving coefficient has degree at least r+2, even if its final
bare row is not r. Common contour gaps and uniform local operator bounds turn
